<title>NEW ZEALAND: Fletcher's Piakau-1 producing 1,400 bpd.</title>
<headline>Fletcher's Piakau-1 producing 1,400 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fletcher Challenge on Thursday reported oil flows of about 1,400 barrels a day from its Piakau-1 well in Taranaki.</p>
<p>The company said that during a five-hour production test on Wednesday, the well's flow rate was about 1,400 barrels with a gas to oil ratio of about 1000 standard cubic feet of gas to each barrel.</p>
<p>The side-tracked well was sunk to re-test the potential of the Tikorangi limestone in the Piakau segment of the Ahuroa-Piakau prospect.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
